# AVIATONLY Lead Messaging CRM

Buyer–seller messaging is **lead-scoped**, not a generic contacts chat.

One **open lead** = one conversation thread for a buyer + listing. Messages feed the CRM (`Lead`, `LeadActivity`, lead workspace) and the **Messages** inbox (`/dashboard/seller/messages`, `/dashboard/messages`).

Related rules: `05-aviatonly-leads-offers-crm.mdc`, `05-aviatonly-buy-pages.mdc`, `02-aviatonly-dashboard-architecture.mdc`, `04-aviatonly-ui-rules.mdc`, `AGENTS.md`.

## Current state (interim)

- `AircraftEnquiryPanel` — UI only; toast on submit, no persistence
- `createLeadAction` / `createLeadRecord` — exist; not wired from buy page
- `/dashboard/seller/messages` — placeholder `RoleWorkspacePage`
- No `LeadMessage` Prisma model yet
- Template `dashboard/apps/chat` — **do not wire**; mock generic chat violates CRM anti-patterns

Buy detail route: `/dashboard/buy/[listingSlug]` (`/buy/[registration]` redirects there).

## Product principles

- Messaging is tied to **leads and listings**, not standalone contacts.
- **Reuse open lead** for same buyer + listing (status not `CLOSED` or `UNQUALIFIED`); do not create a new lead per message.
- **Internal notes** (`NOTE_ADDED`, `internalNotes`) stay separate from buyer-visible messages.
- **Closed leads**: thread read-only; composer disabled.
- Auth required to send; resolve `listingId` / `sellerId` server-side only.
- MVP: server actions + `router.refresh()` or ~30s poll in open thread — no WebSockets until persistence is solid.

## Anti-patterns (do not build)

- Generic CRM contacts module disconnected from listings
- Reusing `ChatContext`, `/api/chat`, or template chat fetchers
- Storing messages only in `Lead.message` or `LeadActivity.message` (need `LeadMessage` table)
- Client-only send with toast and no server action
- Exposing `internalNotes` in message threads
- New lead on every message for the same listing
- Trusting client-provided `sellerId` or `buyerId`

## Domain model (Prisma)

### `LeadMessage` (new)

- `id`, `leadId`, `senderId`, `body`, `createdAt`
- Indexes: `[leadId, createdAt]`, `[senderId]`

### Extend `Lead`

- `lastMessageAt DateTime?`
- `sellerLastReadAt DateTime?`
- `buyerLastReadAt DateTime?`
- Relation: `messages LeadMessage[]`

### Domain (`src/lib/aviatonly/domain/`)

- Add `LeadActivityType.MESSAGE_SENT` — mirror each posted message in activity timeline
- `lead-message.ts` — validate body (trim, min/max length, reject empty)

### Server (`src/lib/aviatonly/server/lead-messages.ts`)

| Function | Responsibility |
|----------|----------------|
| `findOpenLeadForBuyerListing(buyerId, listingId)` | Reuse thread if lead still open |
| `createLeadWithInitialMessage(...)` | Tx: Lead + first message + `LEAD_CREATED` + `MESSAGE_SENT` activities |
| `appendLeadMessage(leadId, senderId, body)` | Auth, insert, update `lastMessageAt`, activity mirror |
| `queryLeadThreadsForUser(userId, role)` | Inbox rows for seller or buyer |
| `queryLeadMessages(leadId, cursor?)` | Paginated thread |
| `markLeadThreadRead(leadId, viewerId)` | Update read watermark |

Reuse `assertCanAccessLead` / `assertCanManageLead` from `src/lib/aviatonly/server/authorization.ts`.

**First seller reply**: set `lastContactedAt`; optional auto `NEW` → `CONTACTED` (mirror `logLeadBuyerResponseRecord` behaviour).

## Routes

```text
/dashboard/buy/[listingSlug]           → enquiry panel creates/reopens lead thread
/dashboard/seller/messages             → seller inbox (two-pane)
/dashboard/seller/messages/[leadId]    → deep link to thread
/dashboard/messages                    → buyer inbox
/dashboard/messages/[leadId]           → buyer thread deep link
/dashboard/seller/leads/[leadId]       → embed Messages tab + link to inbox
```

Add buyer **Messages** nav item in `src/lib/auth/navigation.ts` when Phase D starts.

